# Engineering Workflow

Human-readable: `.cursor/rules-readme/09-engineering-workflow.md`

## Purpose

Define the standard engineering workflow for implementing features, fixing bugs, performing refactoring, writing documentation, and collaborating within the project.

**How do we build it?** Planning identifies work ([`docs/planning/README.md`](../../docs/planning/README.md)); this standard executes it.

A **consistent workflow** improves code quality, maintainability, collaboration, and long-term project health. This standard guides **human developers and AI assistants** alike — work gets done the same way regardless of who writes the code.

This is the **capstone engineering standard**. It complements — not replaces — the specialized standards in `.cursor/rules/`.

## Development Philosophy

We optimize for:

- **Readability** — code and docs that teach, not obscure
- **Maintainability** — structures that survive team and time changes
- **Consistency** — one way to do common things across the monorepo
- **Incremental delivery** — small, reviewable steps over big-bang releases
- **Long-term quality** — production-ready patterns from day one
- **Knowledge sharing** — every change should help future readers learn

This project is **educational and production-oriented** — code should be correct *and* instructive.

## Core Principles

| Principle | Meaning |
| --------- | ------- |
| Understand before implementing | Know the problem, constraints, and acceptance criteria first |
| Read before writing | Search existing code before adding new code |
| Reuse before creating | Extend what exists — packages, patterns, utilities |
| Keep changes focused | One logical change per branch and PR |
| Leave it better | Fix small issues you touch; don't drive-by refactor unrelated code |
| Document important decisions | ADRs and docs for anything costly to reverse |
| Think before coding | Threat model, architecture, and trade-offs before typing |
| Optimize after measurement | Profile first — see `03-coding-standards.mdc` and `06-architecture.mdc` |
| Prefer incremental improvements | Small, reviewable steps over big-bang rewrites |

